  "description": "Below is a concise snapshot of the current and upcoming releases for the major browsers we track.\n\nChrome (access its experimental flags at\u202fchrome://flags) is on version\u202f108, built on the Blink engine\u202f108.0 and released on\u202f2023\u201108\u201131; the official release notes are available at\u202fhttps://chromereleases.googleblog.com/2023/08/stable-channel-update-for-desktop.html, and this build is marked as **current**. The next beta, Chrome\u202f109, also runs Blink\u202f109.0, went live on\u202f2023\u201109\u201128, and its notes can be read at\u202fhttps://chromereleases.googleblog.com/2023/09/stable-channel-update-for-desktop.html.\n\nFirefox (its configuration page is\u202fabout:config) has a current stable release, Firefox\u202f118, powered by Gecko\u202f118.0 and dated\u202f2023\u201109\u201126; the changelog is posted at\u202fhttps://www.mozilla.org/en-US/firefox/118.0/releasenotes/, with a status of **current**. The forthcoming beta, Firefox\u202f119, continues with Gecko\u202f119.0, was released on\u202f2023\u201110\u201131, and its notes are at\u202fhttps://www.mozilla.org/en-US/firefox/119.0/releasenotes/, marked as **beta**.\n\nSafari (preferences are adjusted via\u202fabout:preferences#advanced) is currently at version\u202f16.6, using the WebKit engine\u202f615.5; it was released on\u202f2023\u201109\u201120 and the release notes are hosted at\u202fhttps://developer.apple.com/documentation/safari-release-notes/safari-16_6-release-notes, with a **current** status. The iOS counterpart, Safari\u202fiOS\u202f16.6, mirrors the same WebKit\u202f615.5 engine, release date and notes, and is likewise **current**.\n\nEdge (experimental flags are found at\u202fedge://flags) follows a similar cadence to Chrome. Its stable channel, Edge\u202f108, runs on Blink\u202f108.0, launched on\u202f2023\u201108\u201131, with details at\u202fhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/releasenotes/stable-channel#release-1080, and is listed as **current**. The beta, Edge\u202f109, also uses Blink\u202f109.0, was released on\u202f2023\u201109\u201127, and its notes are at\u202fhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/releasenotes/stable-channel#release-1090, marked as **beta**.",
